WEBVTT

00:00:06.006 --> 00:00:08.008
[upbeat music playing]

00:00:10.886 --> 00:00:11.887
<i>♪ Oh oh ♪</i>

00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:14.348
<i>♪ Oh oh ♪</i>

00:00:14.431 --> 00:00:16.058
♪ <i>Out of the blue </i>♪

00:00:16.141 --> 00:00:18.227
♪ <i>You changed your mind </i>♪

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:19.561
♪ <i>Nothing's real </i>♪

00:00:19.645 --> 00:00:21.647
♪ <i>I didn't change mine </i>♪

00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:23.732
<i>♪ We used to dance... ♪</i>

00:00:23.815 --> 00:00:24.942
Hi!

00:00:25.901 --> 00:00:27.736
♪ <i> We used to laugh... </i>♪

00:00:27.819 --> 00:00:29.404
I'm gonna take this.

00:00:29.488 --> 00:00:33.033
♪ <i> You swore we never stopped dancing </i>♪

00:00:33.116 --> 00:00:36.203
♪<i> You felt all the same feelings </i>♪

00:00:36.286 --> 00:00:37.329
Good deal.

00:00:37.955 --> 00:00:39.122
Thank you for picking me up.

00:00:40.666 --> 00:00:41.583
♪ <i>Way </i>♪

00:00:44.378 --> 00:00:45.546
[phone ringing]

00:00:48.382 --> 00:00:49.216
Hi.

00:00:49.299 --> 00:00:51.051
<i>How's it going? How was your flight?</i>

00:00:51.134 --> 00:00:53.011
Long, of course. You know?

00:00:53.470 --> 00:00:54.846
How are you? What's going on?

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:58.433
<i>Uh, not much.</i>
<i>Just got back from practice. Um...</i>

00:00:59.226 --> 00:01:01.270
<i>Not much else.</i>
<i>What are you up to the rest of the day?</i>

00:01:01.353 --> 00:01:03.397
-I'm going to head into the office.
-[Nick]<i> Nice.</i>

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:04.565
Well, I miss you,

00:01:04.648 --> 00:01:09.403
and I hope that we can see each other,
sooner than later and not go too long.

00:01:09.486 --> 00:01:11.530
<i>Yeah, well, once we figure it out,</i>

00:01:11.613 --> 00:01:14.741
<i>once the season's over,</i>
<i>probably my first stop will be LA.</i>

00:01:14.825 --> 00:01:16.618
I love you

00:01:16.702 --> 00:01:19.788
and have a good game,
and I'll talk to you soon, okay?

00:01:20.330 --> 00:01:22.958
<i>-Talk to you. I love you. Bye.</i>
-Okay, I love you. Bye.

00:01:23.542 --> 00:01:26.461
[Heather] <i>The upside about being</i>
<i>a real estate agent is the flexible hours.</i>

00:01:26.545 --> 00:01:29.881
I've been gone for about a week,
I was visiting my hot man.

00:01:29.965 --> 00:01:32.134
He plays professional hockey in Slovakia.

00:01:32.217 --> 00:01:34.344
He's working basically full-time,

00:01:34.428 --> 00:01:39.182
so I'm kinda the one who has to leave,
go see him, and make that work.

00:01:39.266 --> 00:01:42.686
It's hard because if you don't work
and hustle, you don't get paid.

00:01:42.769 --> 00:01:44.563
♪ <i>Ready or not </i>♪

00:01:44.646 --> 00:01:45.731
♪ <i>Here I come </i>♪

00:01:45.814 --> 00:01:49.359
♪<i> Oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh </i>♪

00:01:49.443 --> 00:01:52.404
<i>♪ Feel my power, power ♪</i>

00:01:54.823 --> 00:01:56.825
[vocalizing]

00:02:00.746 --> 00:02:01.955
<i>♪ Hey ♪</i>

00:02:02.039 --> 00:02:04.583
[vocalizing]

00:02:07.461 --> 00:02:08.670
<i>♪ Hey ♪</i>

00:02:08.754 --> 00:02:12.799
This is that house that looks like
an eighties porn star built it.

00:02:12.883 --> 00:02:14.259
[Brett] So why are we looking at it?

00:02:14.343 --> 00:02:16.386
-[woman] It's just a silly really house.
-[Brett] It's your dream house?

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:18.388
-No, I was telling--
-You'll put it on your vision board?

00:02:18.805 --> 00:02:21.475
I had a vision board for my relationship
and it worked.

00:02:21.558 --> 00:02:22.768
-Aw!
-[Brett] Okay.

00:02:22.851 --> 00:02:24.102
-[woman] That's so cute.
-[Maya] I know.

00:02:24.186 --> 00:02:25.020
Hey!

00:02:25.103 --> 00:02:26.021
Hey, girl!

00:02:26.938 --> 00:02:28.231
[Maya] So are you excited to be back?

00:02:28.315 --> 00:02:30.692
She's so excited she forgot
her computer to work.

00:02:30.776 --> 00:02:31.652
[chuckles]

00:02:31.735 --> 00:02:34.613
I just came to see you girls.
I'm not working today. [chuckles]

00:02:34.696 --> 00:02:36.239
I just got back, girl.

00:02:36.323 --> 00:02:38.033
-[Maya] How was it?
-[Heather] It was good.

00:02:38.116 --> 00:02:39.910
I mean, I got to be with my love.

00:02:39.993 --> 00:02:41.328
I'm sorry. What is he?

00:02:41.411 --> 00:02:43.955
-He's a hockey player.
-Oh, got it. Oh, cool!

00:02:44.039 --> 00:02:46.041
And he's sexy and beautiful,
so that helps.

00:02:46.124 --> 00:02:48.001
My boyfriend is seven years
younger than me.

00:02:48.085 --> 00:02:51.797
<i>He got asked to go play with the KHL,</i>
<i>which is the Kontinental Hockey League.</i>

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:54.716
He was living out in California.
That's when we met.

00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:56.176
<i>He was playing for a team here.</i>

00:02:56.259 --> 00:02:59.262
I think a lot of men think
that I'm, like, their little Barbie doll.

00:02:59.346 --> 00:03:01.223
You know, I have to be a certain way,
act a certain way,

00:03:01.306 --> 00:03:04.643
and he's the first guy
that's ever, like, really let me myself.

00:03:04.726 --> 00:03:06.687
When I'm with him, it's amazing.

00:03:06.770 --> 00:03:09.898
[Chrishell] But aren't a lot of them,
like, they have to put in teeth, right?

00:03:09.981 --> 00:03:13.443
[Heather] Yeah, he lost, like,
half of his two front teeth.

00:03:13.527 --> 00:03:15.946
-Yeah, but I think it's sexy.
-Eek.

00:03:16.029 --> 00:03:19.074
Did you just say he lost two of his teeth
and you think it's sexy?

00:03:19.157 --> 00:03:21.451
Oh, I think it's so hot
when a man looks like that.

00:03:21.535 --> 00:03:23.245
Yeah. Do you want a hockey man, girl?

00:03:23.328 --> 00:03:27.124
They had to have all of their teeth.
That's my only criteria.

00:03:27.207 --> 00:03:30.919
[Christine]<i> Heather's been working at</i>
<i>the Oppenheim Group for almost four years.</i>

00:03:31.002 --> 00:03:32.754
<i>She started right before I did.</i>

00:03:32.838 --> 00:03:36.174
I don't like Heather as a person,
and I get annoyed by Heather all the time.

00:03:36.258 --> 00:03:39.678
It's just because of the way she looks,
because of the way she dresses,

00:03:39.761 --> 00:03:41.263
because of the way she speaks,

00:03:41.346 --> 00:03:45.100
it's because of the lack of wheels
turning up there.

00:03:45.767 --> 00:03:47.769
-Is he moving here or are you--
-He's not gonna move here.

00:03:47.853 --> 00:03:49.438
He can't, 'cause he has to train.

00:03:49.938 --> 00:03:51.481
I mean, he did really well over there,

00:03:51.565 --> 00:03:54.359
so I know they're gonna want him back
and offer him something.

00:03:54.443 --> 00:03:55.402
It's heartbreaking.

00:03:55.485 --> 00:03:57.654
-You got to drink.
-I know, I need a cocktail.

00:03:57.738 --> 00:03:59.698
[Mary] We should get drinks.
My birthday's coming up.

00:03:59.781 --> 00:04:03.785
Oh, wait! That's right! That's right.
Okay, when's your birthday?

00:04:03.869 --> 00:04:06.163
-The 29th.
-Mine's the 21st.

00:04:06.246 --> 00:04:08.540
We should do, like,
a joint birthday party or something.

00:04:08.623 --> 00:04:10.625
That'd be awesome. Oh, yeah!

00:04:10.709 --> 00:04:12.878
-That would be fun. That would be fun.
-Yeah.

00:04:13.795 --> 00:04:15.672
What's up with you? How's the hubby?

00:04:15.756 --> 00:04:18.008
I'm tired between flying and working.

00:04:18.091 --> 00:04:20.677
And, you know,
it's a little bit challenging,

00:04:20.761 --> 00:04:23.013
because I'm spending my time
between Miami and LA,

00:04:23.096 --> 00:04:26.183
you know, trying to do stuff there,
and obviously have clients here.

00:04:26.266 --> 00:04:29.144
But it's good. Like, he comes
to see me when he can.

00:04:29.227 --> 00:04:31.271
He's super busy with work,
but I'm happy.

00:04:31.354 --> 00:04:32.898
Like, it's good. Yeah.

00:04:32.981 --> 00:04:35.150
My situation is similar to Heather's.

00:04:35.233 --> 00:04:38.862
We are doing long distance
with the guys we love.

00:04:38.945 --> 00:04:40.864
With her, it's a little bit different.

00:04:40.947 --> 00:04:42.991
She cannot just go on a weekend
to see him.

00:04:43.074 --> 00:04:45.368
It's 13 hours of flights.

00:04:45.911 --> 00:04:48.121
[Christine] Heather,
get on your computer and do some work!

00:04:48.205 --> 00:04:49.831
[scoffs] I don't have it, girl.

00:04:50.332 --> 00:04:53.001
-Can I borrow yours?
-No, 'cause you might not give it back.

00:04:53.668 --> 00:04:55.420
Of course I would give your computer back.

00:04:55.504 --> 00:04:57.047
[dogs barking]

00:04:57.130 --> 00:04:59.925
-[Chrishell] The bitches are fighting.
-[Maya] Which ones?

00:05:00.008 --> 00:05:01.009
[chuckles]

00:05:01.092 --> 00:05:02.844
<i>♪ Hold up</i>
<i>I'm just getting started ♪</i>

00:05:02.928 --> 00:05:05.722
<i>♪ When I have to roll up</i>
<i>You know it's a party ♪</i>

00:05:05.806 --> 00:05:08.225
<i>♪ Let my hair down</i>
<i>Having some fun ♪</i>

00:05:08.308 --> 00:05:10.060
<i>♪ Hands up</i>
<i>Marching to the beat of my drum ♪</i>

00:05:10.143 --> 00:05:13.230
<i>♪ They're my ladies</i>
<i>Around the globe ♪</i>

00:05:13.313 --> 00:05:14.981
<i>♪ Live it up</i>
<i>Live it up ♪</i>

00:05:15.065 --> 00:05:17.984
<i>♪ All my ladies from the show ♪</i>

00:05:18.068 --> 00:05:20.070
<i>♪ Making moves and we just don't stop ♪</i>

00:05:20.153 --> 00:05:22.614
<i>♪ My ladies around the globe ♪</i>

00:05:22.697 --> 00:05:24.533
<i>♪Work it, love it, live it up ♪</i>

00:05:24.616 --> 00:05:27.452
-So sorry I'm running a little late.
-No problem at all.

00:05:27.536 --> 00:05:29.079
-How are you?
-I'm good, thank you.

00:05:29.162 --> 00:05:31.373
-Thank you for seeing me.
-Of course!

00:05:31.456 --> 00:05:33.792
-This house, I'm so excited to show you.
-Yes!

00:05:36.545 --> 00:05:38.171
-[Mary] Close to everything.
-[woman] Oh, wow!

00:05:38.255 --> 00:05:41.258
-Yes. It's huge!
-[Mary] This is why I wanted to bring you.

00:05:41.341 --> 00:05:42.217
[chuckles]

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:46.263
I would never think
that this house could be this big.

00:05:46.346 --> 00:05:50.600
Yeah, so this is about
just under 5,000 square feet.

00:05:50.684 --> 00:05:52.769
It's kind of what I think
you're looking for.

00:05:52.853 --> 00:05:57.482
[Mary]<i> I love the LA real estate market</i>
<i>because I'm competitive.</i>

00:05:58.066 --> 00:06:01.319
I wanna win. I wanna get
my clients their home,

00:06:01.403 --> 00:06:04.906
I wanna get the highest price
for my sellers, beating out other buyers,

00:06:04.990 --> 00:06:07.868
<i>making sure your client is the one</i>
<i>that gets their offer accepted.</i>

00:06:07.951 --> 00:06:09.035
It's exhilarating.

00:06:09.119 --> 00:06:11.663
You mentioned you like contemporary,

00:06:11.746 --> 00:06:14.332
high ceilings, natural light,

00:06:15.166 --> 00:06:16.835
and this one is really spectacular.

00:06:16.918 --> 00:06:19.087
I think, they really did a good job,

00:06:19.170 --> 00:06:23.425
of making
a very nice contemporary modern feel,

00:06:23.508 --> 00:06:27.637
but also they have elements
in here, that bring in the warmth.

00:06:28.263 --> 00:06:30.473
-[woman] Yes, like the wood...
-[Mary] So it's not too cold.

00:06:30.557 --> 00:06:32.267
It's definitely my style.

00:06:32.350 --> 00:06:34.269
These are all pocket doors,

00:06:34.352 --> 00:06:38.398
so you can open up
this set of doors and this set of doors,

00:06:38.481 --> 00:06:42.485
and you really get
the whole indoor-outdoor living.

00:06:42.569 --> 00:06:45.363
You get all the natural light
and the breeze that comes in.

00:06:45.447 --> 00:06:47.282
[woman] I really like that.

00:06:47.365 --> 00:06:50.327
-This reminds me of Turkey. Back home.
-Oh, really.

00:06:50.410 --> 00:06:52.412
Whoever built this house
must be from Turkey.

00:06:52.495 --> 00:06:54.164
[Mary chuckles] All the olive trees.

00:06:54.247 --> 00:06:55.332
[woman] Yeah. Exactly.

00:06:55.415 --> 00:06:56.875
See, it's meant to be.

00:06:56.958 --> 00:06:59.920
This is such a perfect house for you.

00:07:00.003 --> 00:07:02.422
So, master bedroom.

00:07:03.131 --> 00:07:03.965
[woman] Big.

00:07:04.215 --> 00:07:06.593
-[Mary] Yes. [chuckles]
-[woman] Beautiful!

00:07:06.676 --> 00:07:10.639
Yes. So you got your own private balcony
off the master suite.

00:07:10.722 --> 00:07:12.974
You told me that every room
has a balcony, right?

00:07:13.058 --> 00:07:17.771
Exactly. Every room has an en suite bath
and its own private balcony.

00:07:17.854 --> 00:07:21.691
So the shower,
see the size of the shower here?

00:07:21.775 --> 00:07:26.696
It's amazing. Dual shower heads.
You got this beautiful tub.

00:07:26.780 --> 00:07:28.615
[woman] Super nice.

00:07:29.658 --> 00:07:34.454
[Mary] And also we have
a little living area up here as well.

00:07:34.537 --> 00:07:36.081
-[woman] Wow.
-[Mary] What do you think?

00:07:36.164 --> 00:07:40.919
It definitely has all the elements that,
you know, we discussed on the phone.

00:07:41.461 --> 00:07:45.256
-I'm 30 now and I need to slow down.
-Okay.

00:07:45.340 --> 00:07:48.468
This will be the home
and hopefully a family inside of it.

00:07:48.551 --> 00:07:52.138
That's the main reason I want to be here,
and also trying to convince my man

00:07:52.222 --> 00:07:53.890
-to maybe have a family one day.
-[chuckles]

00:07:53.974 --> 00:07:55.976
I'll-- I'll handle this part of that.

00:07:56.601 --> 00:08:01.022
I'm glad you love it. I thought, that
this would be right kind of up your alley,

00:08:01.106 --> 00:08:03.149
of what you said you were looking for.

00:08:03.233 --> 00:08:04.401
Perfect.

00:08:04.484 --> 00:08:06.903
-Now I feel more hopeful, you know?
-[chuckles]

00:08:06.987 --> 00:08:08.905
It feels so far away
when you're over there.

00:08:08.989 --> 00:08:10.699
-I think I might take it.
-Really?

00:08:10.782 --> 00:08:13.076
'Cause I know you're looking
for a house, too. You were telling me.

00:08:13.159 --> 00:08:17.664
Romain and I are-- are really thinking
of trying to buy a place,

00:08:17.747 --> 00:08:21.793
so I'm absolutely in love
with this home, too,

00:08:21.876 --> 00:08:23.878
so if you don't get it, I might.
[chuckles]

00:08:23.962 --> 00:08:28.508
<i>♪ Hold on</i>
<i>I just got to let you know ♪</i>

00:08:30.218 --> 00:08:32.595
-I love you.
-I love you.

00:08:34.014 --> 00:08:37.142
<i>♪ Higher and I can't get enough ♪</i>

00:08:37.225 --> 00:08:40.103
<i>♪ I want reach out and touch it ♪</i>

00:08:40.437 --> 00:08:41.896
Perfect, thank you.

00:08:43.106 --> 00:08:43.982
Thank you.

00:08:44.649 --> 00:08:45.942
This place is beautiful.

00:08:46.484 --> 00:08:50.030
-Nice and romantic for our anniversary.
-Yeah.

00:08:50.113 --> 00:08:52.157
-One year already.
-I know.

00:08:53.241 --> 00:08:55.702
I'm glad you ate the hat on me.

00:08:56.202 --> 00:08:58.204
[chuckles] What?

00:08:58.288 --> 00:09:00.915
Romain has a very good vocabulary.

00:09:00.999 --> 00:09:04.461
You just can't understand,
what he says a lot of the time,

00:09:04.544 --> 00:09:06.463
because he just has a very thick accent.

00:09:06.546 --> 00:09:09.424
I think he's doing very well.
Better than me with French, anyway.

00:09:09.507 --> 00:09:11.134
You hit hard on me.

00:09:12.010 --> 00:09:13.720
-What?
-Our first date.

00:09:14.137 --> 00:09:17.849
I know certain words like <i>santé.</i>

00:09:17.932 --> 00:09:19.642
Bottoms up, like cheers.

00:09:19.726 --> 00:09:21.311
Of course, I'm the one who knows that one.

00:09:21.394 --> 00:09:23.146
I hit hard on you?

00:09:23.229 --> 00:09:24.814
Yeah. [chuckles]

00:09:24.898 --> 00:09:27.275
-You hit on me.
-Yeah, maybe.

00:09:27.358 --> 00:09:31.154
You reached over and grabbed my hand,
and I was like, "Hell, yeah."

00:09:31.237 --> 00:09:32.572
And then you kissed me.

00:09:32.655 --> 00:09:33.948
It was meant to be.

00:09:34.032 --> 00:09:35.366
It was all you.

00:09:35.450 --> 00:09:36.493
[Romain laughs]

00:09:36.576 --> 00:09:38.328
-Hi.
-Hi. How are you?

00:09:38.411 --> 00:09:39.788
May I get you something to drink?

00:09:39.871 --> 00:09:41.539
Do you have espresso martinis?

00:09:41.623 --> 00:09:43.208
-Espresso martini?
-[Mary] Yeah, please.

00:09:43.291 --> 00:09:45.376
And would you like to order?

00:09:45.460 --> 00:09:48.588
No, I'm just gonna do a margarita.

00:09:48.671 --> 00:09:51.883
I don't know how to say it,
but the pappardelle with the wild boar.

00:09:51.966 --> 00:09:53.676
<i>Nastria cinghiale.</i>

00:09:53.760 --> 00:09:55.345
So much more beautiful when you say it.

00:09:55.428 --> 00:09:58.515
<i>Bene,</i> then the <i>nastria</i>
and the pizza margharita.<i> Grazie.</i>

00:09:58.598 --> 00:10:00.225
-Thank you.
<i>-Prego. Salute.</i>

00:10:02.811 --> 00:10:04.687
I've been married twice before.

00:10:04.771 --> 00:10:06.648
<i>The first husband has passed away,</i>

00:10:06.731 --> 00:10:08.983
<i>and the second husband,</i>
<i>it just didn't work out.</i>

00:10:09.067 --> 00:10:10.693
<i>It wasn't the right relationship to be in.</i>

00:10:10.777 --> 00:10:13.238
Never thought I wanted
to get married again.

00:10:14.531 --> 00:10:15.907
How's your work going?

00:10:15.990 --> 00:10:18.451
So the boys took us up to see this house.

00:10:18.535 --> 00:10:21.204
It's one
of the most amazing properties I've seen.

00:10:21.287 --> 00:10:23.498
[Jason]<i> It's over 4,000 square feet,</i>
<i>this rooftop deck.</i>

00:10:23.581 --> 00:10:26.543
<i>The largest rooftop deck</i>
<i>of any property ever listed in the hills.</i>

00:10:26.626 --> 00:10:27.794
You have to come see it.

00:10:27.877 --> 00:10:29.420
It's 40 million dollars.

00:10:29.504 --> 00:10:33.133
It is one of the most epic homes
in the hills right now.

00:10:33.216 --> 00:10:36.177
I'm thinking about
which buyer I'm gonna get.

00:10:36.261 --> 00:10:40.098
That's gonna be a war
between you guys to find a buyer, right?

00:10:40.181 --> 00:10:41.391
Oh, I'm winning.

00:10:41.474 --> 00:10:42.684
[laughs]

00:10:43.268 --> 00:10:44.269
For sure.

00:10:44.352 --> 00:10:47.147
-Espresso martini.
-Thank you. Oh, it looks good.

00:10:48.231 --> 00:10:49.065
<i>Prego.</i>

00:10:49.149 --> 00:10:51.276
